{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>I will advise you</b> — Three times in the Masorah: here, and the other two: בלעם לכה איעצך, and וכי איעצך לא תשמע אלי. For the prophecy of Balaam is linked to the prophecy of Moses. And the Sages said: 'And there arose not a prophet again in Israel like Moses' — but among the nations of the world, one did arise. I received that its meaning is: arose for a time, i.e., for the moment, just as it spoke for the moment and not continuously. And the other: וכי איעצך לא תשמע אלי — concerning Zedekiah, whom Jeremiah advised to go out to the officers of the king of Babylon. Moses, who listened to the advice of Jethro — it is said of him: 'he shall come to his place in peace.' But Zedekiah, who did not listen to the advice of Jeremiah — was exiled from his place."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:32.516902246Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}